-- title:
--   Vélu quotient of a nodal cubic by an odd-order point
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with decidable equality and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ given by coefficients $a_1,\dots,a_6$, assumed nodal in the sense that its discriminant satisfies $\Delta = 0$ while $c_4 \neq 0$. Let $n$ be an odd natural number and let $Q$ be a point of the associated affine curve `W.toAffine` whose order in the group of points is exactly $n$. Form the finite set $S \subseteq F \times F$ consisting of the coordinates of the multiples $k \bullet Q$ for $k$ ranging over the integers from $1$ to $\lfloor n/2 \rfloor = (n-1)/2$, where the point at infinity contributes the pair $(0,0)$ and an affine point contributes its $(x,y)$. The Vélu quotient of $W$ by $S$ is the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S} t(P)$ and $a_6$ replaced by $a_6 - b_2\sum_{P\in S} t(P) - 7\sum_{P\in S} w(P)$, the sums being those of Vélu's terms `veluT` and `veluW` over $S$. The assertion is the conjunction of three identities for this quotient curve: its $c_4$ equals $n^4 c_4(W)$, its $c_6$ equals $n^6 c_6(W)$, and its discriminant is $0$ (with $n$ read in $F$).
--
--   This is the closed form of Vélu's isogeny formulas in the degenerate multiplicative case: quotienting a nodal cubic by the cyclic subgroup of order $n$ generated by a point of the nonsingular locus returns a nodal cubic again, and the resulting model differs from the original one by the scaling $u = 1/n$, the hypothesis $c_4 \neq 0$ excluding the cuspidal degeneration. It feeds [`WeierstrassCurve.valuation_veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_c4_of_multiplicative`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.valuation_veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_c4_of_multiplicative), which handles the multiplicative-reduction case in the comparison of invariants of a curve and of its quotient by a point of prime order.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_c4_c6_discriminant_of_nodal.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_Velu
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_OddOrderSummingSet

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine

theorem WeierstrassCurve.veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_c4_c6_discriminant_of_nodal
    {F : Type*} [Field F] [DecidableEq F] (W : WeierstrassCurve F)
    (hΔ : W.Δ = 0) (hc₄ : W.c₄ ≠ 0)
    {n : ℕ} (hn : Odd n)
    (Q : W.toAffine.Point) (hQord : addOrderOf Q = n) :
    (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (n / 2))).c₄ = (n : F) ^ 4 * W.c₄ ∧
    (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (n / 2))).c₆ = (n : F) ^ 6 * W.c₆ ∧
    (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (n / 2))).Δ = 0 := by sorry
